WEBVTT

00:41.625 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:44.044 --> 00:46.755
WOOSONG HOSPITAL

00:56.348 --> 00:57.307
EMERGENCY ROOM

01:06.692 --> 01:07.734
Are you okay?

01:10.445 --> 01:11.780
Are you all right?

01:25.502 --> 01:27.280
Hey, Eun-ho.

01:28.839 --> 01:31.049
What… Eun-ho!

01:32.134 --> 01:33.051
Where did she go?

01:36.680 --> 01:37.764
Clear the way!

01:41.602 --> 01:43.437
- What…
- Are you family?

01:43.520 --> 01:45.314
Well, my friend is in there.

01:45.397 --> 01:47.774
- Hyeon Woo-seok is in there, right?
- You can't just barge in.

01:47.858 --> 01:50.068
I told you, I'm his friend.

01:51.069 --> 01:53.697
I just need to check on him.
It'll only take a few minutes.

01:53.780 --> 01:55.741
- Hey, you can't!
- Please!

01:56.658 --> 01:58.827
Aren't you Si-yeol?

01:59.494 --> 02:01.163
Mr. Hyeon.

02:01.246 --> 02:02.247
How's Woo-seok?

02:02.998 --> 02:04.374
Is Woo-seok okay?

02:05.000 --> 02:06.627
What is happening?

02:06.710 --> 02:08.795
Why did Woo-seok suddenly collapse?

02:09.421 --> 02:12.049
Is he really going to die?
Then what about Si-yeol?

02:14.343 --> 02:17.846
Say something! I'm sure you showed up
because you have something to say.

02:18.347 --> 02:23.352
Did you think tampering with human fate
was a trivial matter?

02:25.062 --> 02:25.937
What?

02:26.021 --> 02:27.439
Charging 150 joules.

02:27.981 --> 02:29.024
Clear!

02:29.107 --> 02:30.942
Charging 200 joules. Two, clear!

02:38.158 --> 02:39.868
Sinus rhythm is back.

02:42.204 --> 02:43.789
- Start a saline drip, wide open.
- On it.

02:43.872 --> 02:47.292
He's not dead. Not yet.

02:47.376 --> 02:50.420
Not yet? What does that mean?

02:51.046 --> 02:53.382
He will eventually die.

02:54.591 --> 02:56.968
Just not today.

02:57.052 --> 02:59.721
That's the fate

03:01.014 --> 03:02.641
you gave him.

03:05.227 --> 03:09.147
Does that mean Si-yeol's fate was…

03:09.231 --> 03:12.901
To rise high, but burn out quickly.

03:12.984 --> 03:15.987
That was the fate
Kang Si-yeol was born with.

03:16.822 --> 03:20.534
On the other hand,
a long but difficult life

03:20.617 --> 03:24.037
was the fate Hyeon Woo-seok was born with.

03:28.417 --> 03:30.460
Then what am I supposed to do?

03:31.002 --> 03:32.838
I don't like either option.

03:34.131 --> 03:37.384
I don't want to make Si-yeol
watch his friend die in his place

03:37.467 --> 03:40.137
or return to his original life and die.

03:41.471 --> 03:43.265
There must be another way.

03:43.348 --> 03:45.225
Change fate, twist it, whatever.

03:45.308 --> 03:49.146
If they were given such a crappy fate,
there must be a loophole or something!

03:49.229 --> 03:52.774
You still haven't learned a thing.

03:53.525 --> 03:56.111
You recklessly tampered with human fate,

03:56.778 --> 04:00.157
caused an innocent man to die again,

04:00.657 --> 04:04.953
and now you seek cheap tricks
to deceive Heaven?

04:05.787 --> 04:07.956
That's right. I'll find a way.

04:08.999 --> 04:11.710
That's how I've survived until now,

04:11.793 --> 04:16.465
and I have no intention
of ever accepting such a crappy fate.

04:21.178 --> 04:23.680
The only thing I can give you now…

04:28.894 --> 04:30.020
is this.

04:38.528 --> 04:40.280
When this season ends,

04:40.822 --> 04:47.162
Kang Si-yeol's true fate is to die
before he sees another winter.

04:47.788 --> 04:51.541
So, before Hyeon Woo-seok
dies in his place,

04:52.167 --> 04:56.004
fix this twisted fate
with your own two hands.

05:15.816 --> 05:18.360
What on earth
am I supposed to fix with this?

05:18.443 --> 05:20.862
You already know

05:20.946 --> 05:23.657
what that dagger is

05:23.740 --> 05:26.117
and what you should do.

05:35.335 --> 05:37.796
Stab him with this. You have to.

05:38.421 --> 05:41.091
Commit an unforgivable sin,

05:41.716 --> 05:44.469
and turn all your cultivated virtue
to nothing.

05:45.887 --> 05:48.348
If you stab your beloved with that dagger,

05:49.182 --> 05:51.268
the twisted fate will return to its place,

05:51.351 --> 05:54.479
and you can return to being
a nine-tailed fox again.

05:56.273 --> 05:57.440
However,

05:57.983 --> 06:01.152
if you leave this twisted fate as it is

06:01.778 --> 06:05.740
and a man who shouldn't die
ends up dying instead…

06:07.868 --> 06:09.244
I will personally

06:09.327 --> 06:13.415
end your fate with that dagger.

06:14.374 --> 06:15.876
Then, no matter what you do,

06:15.959 --> 06:19.129
you will never return to being
a nine-tailed fox.

06:20.046 --> 06:22.132
You'll live out your life

06:23.383 --> 06:26.344
as a human forever, like you are now.

06:35.979 --> 06:40.609
EPISODE 10
FROM CHANCE TO DESTINY

06:41.359 --> 06:43.570
His heart rate is back to normal,

06:43.653 --> 06:46.948
and thankfully, he woke right up.

06:47.616 --> 06:49.659
We were lucky he got
immediate emergency care.

06:50.285 --> 06:51.620
They said it could've been worse.

06:52.704 --> 06:55.206
That's such a relief.

06:56.625 --> 06:58.209
You must have been quite shocked too.

06:58.293 --> 06:59.419
Yes.

07:00.253 --> 07:02.088
It was all so sudden.

07:02.964 --> 07:04.299
Si-yeol.

07:05.592 --> 07:07.928
Thanks for rushing over,
even at this hour.

07:09.012 --> 07:10.180
I appreciate it.

07:12.182 --> 07:13.934
I wish you could see Woo-seok,

07:14.017 --> 07:16.645
but they're running further tests
on him right now.

07:17.562 --> 07:20.565
Is there another problem?

07:21.650 --> 07:24.694
It's nothing like that.
Just standard procedure.

07:25.236 --> 07:28.740
Judging by his condition,
I don't expect any lasting damage.

07:29.282 --> 07:30.283
Don't worry too much.

07:31.660 --> 07:32.744
Okay.

07:35.538 --> 07:38.124
Anyway, I should get going.

07:41.002 --> 07:43.046
I'll let Woo-seok know you stopped by.

07:43.129 --> 07:44.881
- See you around.
- Okay.

08:18.123 --> 08:20.917
It's a relief that he's still alive.

08:23.420 --> 08:24.546
Yeah.

08:25.714 --> 08:28.842
I'd feel much better
if I could've seen his face.

08:29.968 --> 08:31.344
He should be okay, right?

08:35.348 --> 08:36.683
By the way,

08:37.767 --> 08:41.271
what kind of person
is this Woo-seok anyway?

08:42.856 --> 08:44.065
What?

08:45.316 --> 08:46.443
I'm just curious.

08:47.610 --> 08:49.404
Surely he's someone special

08:49.487 --> 08:52.866
if you'd go as far as to give up
your wish for him?

08:53.908 --> 08:58.038
Even now, you're worrying about him first
instead of how close you came

08:58.121 --> 09:00.123
to never getting your old life back.

09:02.208 --> 09:05.712
You make it sound
like it's some huge deal.

09:07.213 --> 09:09.591
We're just friends.

09:10.967 --> 09:13.470
And friends make sacrifices
for each other.

09:14.554 --> 09:17.682
I get a little upset sometimes,
but I still worry about him.

09:18.641 --> 09:21.061
Come on, what kind of answer is that?

09:21.144 --> 09:23.354
If he's that special to you,

09:23.438 --> 09:26.399
I thought you'd tell me
about some hidden talent

09:26.483 --> 09:28.109
or that he's actually a pretty decent guy.

09:28.193 --> 09:31.446
Is that really all there is to him?

09:34.240 --> 09:35.658
Woo-seok is

09:36.659 --> 09:38.369
kind of a coward.

09:39.788 --> 09:42.165
He's great at giving
but awful at receiving,

09:42.791 --> 09:44.167
and he's a little pathetic too.

09:44.250 --> 09:46.669
He only wants me to see his good side,

09:46.753 --> 09:48.922
so he hides
whenever things don't go his way.

09:49.506 --> 09:50.757
He's got an inferiority complex.

09:50.840 --> 09:51.966
What?

09:52.675 --> 09:54.511
Then why…

09:54.594 --> 09:58.181
But I still like him,
regardless of all that.

09:59.724 --> 10:01.601
I bet Woo-seok feels the same way.

10:02.560 --> 10:04.604
I'm selfish, self-centered,

10:05.230 --> 10:06.815
and totally full of myself.

10:07.357 --> 10:09.859
Woo-seok knows all that about me.

10:09.943 --> 10:12.654
But that's how childhood friends are.

10:13.780 --> 10:15.573
Even though we're pathetic and cowardly,

10:16.116 --> 10:17.200
none of that matters.

10:19.202 --> 10:20.286
I don't really get it.

10:21.788 --> 10:24.999
Shouldn't you dislike each other
if you're all that pathetic and cowardly?

10:25.625 --> 10:27.585
- I think you already know.
- What?

10:27.669 --> 10:28.753
You like me, don't you?

10:29.921 --> 10:32.841
It's not because I'm the best
or somehow special

10:33.424 --> 10:36.427
out of everyone you've ever met
in your long life.

10:37.053 --> 10:40.431
I became special to you
because you like me.

10:44.227 --> 10:48.273
I think that's what it means
to like someone.

10:52.193 --> 10:53.486
What if…

10:55.196 --> 10:59.534
I couldn't go back
to my true form because of you

10:59.617 --> 11:02.162
and had to live as a human forever?

11:03.746 --> 11:05.957
Would I still be able to like you then?

11:07.208 --> 11:08.334
What?

11:08.418 --> 11:11.004
If your friend had really died today,

11:11.629 --> 11:14.215
and you'd lost your chance
to get your fate back forever,

11:14.841 --> 11:18.386
would you still not resent me?

11:19.679 --> 11:21.472
Would you still like me?

11:23.141 --> 11:25.727
Eun-ho, are you okay?

11:26.477 --> 11:28.229
Did something happen earlier?

11:32.942 --> 11:34.110
Nothing happened.

11:35.153 --> 11:36.946
The thought just came to me.

11:38.698 --> 11:41.284
Are you telling me to choose?

11:41.951 --> 11:45.872
Kill Si-yeol, or give up who I am?

11:46.497 --> 11:48.124
It may seem cruel,

11:48.833 --> 11:51.419
but fate simply takes its course.

11:52.295 --> 11:55.882
It does not concern itself
with individual human affairs.

12:01.512 --> 12:03.765
Then why are you telling me to choose?

12:04.891 --> 12:06.434
If the will of Heaven is already set,

12:06.517 --> 12:09.020
you guys should decide
whether to kill him or save him.

12:14.108 --> 12:17.320
I almost fell for your tricks again.

12:17.403 --> 12:19.072
I keep forgetting

12:19.697 --> 12:22.867
that you guys act
like you know everything,

12:22.951 --> 12:24.702
but the truth is, you don't know anything.

12:24.786 --> 12:26.579
You were just trying to trick me

12:26.663 --> 12:29.791
into fixing these twisted
human affairs for you.

12:30.917 --> 12:33.336
But I found another way.

12:34.045 --> 12:36.422
So I'm not making that damn choice.

12:38.007 --> 12:40.385
Once I get my powers back,

12:40.468 --> 12:42.720
saving Si-yeol will be a piece of cake.

12:44.722 --> 12:47.934
I'll just stay by his side
and protect him forever.

12:52.397 --> 12:54.107
I'm suddenly so tired.

12:56.150 --> 12:57.402
Okay.

12:58.027 --> 13:00.238
You must be tired
after rushing out with me like that.

13:00.321 --> 13:03.283
Get some rest.
I'll wake you when we're there.

13:05.660 --> 13:06.619
Si-yeol.

13:08.413 --> 13:09.789
What I said earlier

13:10.540 --> 13:12.458
wasn't just the alcohol talking.

13:13.584 --> 13:14.502
What?

13:14.585 --> 13:18.256
I told you I'd get your life back,
no matter what.

13:18.339 --> 13:19.299
That's a promise.

13:20.258 --> 13:22.552
So don't worry about it.

13:22.635 --> 13:26.639
Get some sleep.
We can worry about that tomorrow.

13:49.537 --> 13:51.581
Si-yeol, wake up! Come on!

13:52.123 --> 13:53.166
What…

13:54.292 --> 13:55.752
What's got into you so early?

13:55.835 --> 13:57.879
We saw yesterday
that we're gaining spiritual power,

13:57.962 --> 14:00.381
and now that we know how,
we need to hurry.

14:00.465 --> 14:03.259
Right.
We have to do good deeds.

14:04.427 --> 14:05.762
Do you have a plan or something?

14:05.845 --> 14:07.972
Technically, it's not doing good deeds.

14:08.056 --> 14:11.100
I'm fixing the misdeeds I committed.

14:11.184 --> 14:13.936
I made a list of everything
that came to mind, so listen.

14:15.772 --> 14:17.440
Chairman Jin of Pyeongchang-dong.

14:18.149 --> 14:21.569
What misdeed did you commit with him?

14:21.652 --> 14:25.406
Was it the late '90s?

14:26.157 --> 14:28.368
There was some land Chairman Jin wanted

14:28.451 --> 14:30.953
that the owner wouldn't sell,
no matter what.

14:31.037 --> 14:33.873
So you forced him to sell it?

14:33.956 --> 14:36.793
Yeah, since I took money
from Chairman Jin,

14:36.876 --> 14:38.378
I had to do my part.

14:39.045 --> 14:40.713
Where was this land anyway?

14:41.923 --> 14:43.132
Pangyo.

14:44.050 --> 14:45.760
What? Pangyo?

14:45.843 --> 14:47.762
How could you--

14:47.845 --> 14:51.057
I didn't know the area would boom.

14:51.140 --> 14:54.519
It was nothing but rice paddies back then.
I should've bought some.

14:54.602 --> 14:55.603
Unbelievable.

14:55.686 --> 14:57.438
Assemblyman Park of Hannam-dong.

14:57.522 --> 15:00.525
He was a real piece of work too.

15:02.944 --> 15:04.237
How does it look?

15:04.320 --> 15:07.281
Will this affect Woo-seok's career?

15:08.491 --> 15:10.076
I looked it up,

15:10.159 --> 15:13.996
and some players overseas play
with an implantable defibrillator.

15:15.415 --> 15:17.667
Does Woo-seok need to go that far?

15:18.292 --> 15:22.296
Well, depending on the cause
of the sudden cardiac arrest,

15:22.380 --> 15:24.632
that might be an option.

15:24.715 --> 15:28.010
We ran tests to figure that out,

15:28.803 --> 15:30.430
but how should I put this?

15:31.431 --> 15:33.474
The results aren't good.

15:36.310 --> 15:37.395
Excuse me?

15:41.441 --> 15:45.236
He has primary cardiac angiosarcoma.

15:46.863 --> 15:48.573
What is that?

15:49.574 --> 15:52.243
Simply put, it's heart cancer.

15:53.286 --> 15:54.829
Heart cancer…

15:58.332 --> 16:02.170
No. Cancer in the heart?
I've never heard of such a thing.

16:02.253 --> 16:06.591
Cancer cells
don't usually form in the heart,

16:06.674 --> 16:08.926
so this is a very rare case.

16:09.010 --> 16:13.514
It accounts for only 0.01%
of all cancer cases.

16:13.598 --> 16:15.057
Doctor!

16:15.558 --> 16:16.976
Didn't you see the news?

16:17.059 --> 16:19.645
Woo-seok just had
a medical check-up for his transfer.

16:19.729 --> 16:21.814
Surely your test is wrong?

16:21.898 --> 16:23.941
Heart cancer is tricky like that.

16:24.025 --> 16:28.404
There are no clear symptoms,
and it's so rare

16:28.488 --> 16:29.655
that it's hard to detect.

16:30.448 --> 16:31.574
How…

16:34.994 --> 16:37.538
Then what do we do now?

16:38.164 --> 16:39.957
There has to be a treatment, right?

16:40.041 --> 16:41.501
We don't care how much it costs--

16:41.584 --> 16:42.710
Am I…

16:44.462 --> 16:45.838
going to die?

16:47.798 --> 16:49.967
It's too late for surgery.

16:50.635 --> 16:53.679
And a transplant isn't a realistic option.

16:56.307 --> 16:57.808
You said it's rare.

16:58.309 --> 17:00.186
So you don't know much
about it either, do you?

17:01.896 --> 17:04.607
You should look into it more
before giving up!

17:04.690 --> 17:06.692
How can you call yourself a doctor?

17:08.236 --> 17:11.239
How much time do I have left?

17:14.659 --> 17:16.118
Six months at most.

17:16.702 --> 17:18.579
It could be less.

17:38.891 --> 17:40.643
What did I do that was so wrong?

17:40.726 --> 17:43.396
I didn't ask for too much.

17:43.896 --> 17:45.773
I didn't ask to live like this forever.

17:45.856 --> 17:48.442
I just wanted to live my dream for a bit.

17:48.526 --> 17:50.570
Why can't I even have that?

17:52.029 --> 17:53.239
Woo-seok.

17:54.657 --> 17:56.409
Something's wrong here.

18:00.204 --> 18:01.163
Dad.

18:02.290 --> 18:04.125
This shouldn't be happening to me.

18:05.626 --> 18:07.545
I know.

18:10.923 --> 18:14.343
Calm down, and let's get retested.

18:15.469 --> 18:17.847
That guy's a total quack.

18:18.472 --> 18:22.018
You've been training since you could walk.

18:22.101 --> 18:25.771
You can play a full match
without getting tired.

18:25.855 --> 18:27.440
How could you have heart problems?

18:27.523 --> 18:29.942
That's just ridiculous.

18:30.026 --> 18:32.278
No. That's not it.

18:37.033 --> 18:40.786
We can't go to another hospital.
We have to keep this a secret, Dad.

18:41.996 --> 18:43.748
- What?
- Pay off the doctor.

18:43.831 --> 18:45.166
Do whatever it takes!

18:46.626 --> 18:48.127
This can't get out.

18:49.337 --> 18:51.380
What are you talking about, Woo-seok?

18:51.464 --> 18:53.424
We need to get you tested again.

18:53.507 --> 18:55.051
Si-yeol…

18:55.134 --> 18:56.552
Forget all that.

18:58.346 --> 19:00.097
I need to see Si-yeol.

19:02.266 --> 19:06.812
So, these are all the misdeeds
you've committed?

19:06.896 --> 19:09.106
No, not exactly--

19:09.190 --> 19:10.399
Right?

19:10.483 --> 19:12.151
I thought the list was too--

19:12.234 --> 19:15.029
I only listed cases since Liberation.
I left out the Joseon era.

19:15.655 --> 19:18.699
We need the clients to still be alive
for us to do anything.

19:18.783 --> 19:21.535
Right. I see.

19:21.619 --> 19:24.372
You sure were diligent about making money.

19:24.455 --> 19:26.999
- Anyway, what do you think?
- What?

19:27.083 --> 19:30.211
Which one should we set right first?

19:30.795 --> 19:32.755
Man, I don't know.

19:33.339 --> 19:34.924
There are just so many.

19:35.007 --> 19:37.093
Even if we just pick a few easy ones,

19:37.176 --> 19:39.762
I think the spiritual power
will build up fast.

19:44.141 --> 19:45.476
Wait.

19:49.313 --> 19:50.648
It's Woo-seok.

20:01.492 --> 20:02.952
It's locked.

20:07.998 --> 20:09.291
Just wait a second.

20:19.677 --> 20:20.886
What's up?

20:20.970 --> 20:23.097
Coach, the field is locked.

20:23.180 --> 20:24.765
What?

20:26.183 --> 20:27.810
Seriously, those guys.

20:28.352 --> 20:30.438
I asked them to just wait a few days.

20:32.690 --> 20:34.608
Pardon? Wait for what?

20:35.234 --> 20:36.610
Never mind.

20:37.236 --> 20:40.781
Look, there's no training today.

20:40.865 --> 20:43.451
So just go home, rest up,
and take care of yourselves.

20:43.534 --> 20:45.953
Another day off?
We just got one yesterday.

20:46.036 --> 20:48.414
You guys aren't in the best shape.

20:48.497 --> 20:51.041
Hey, just do as I say and tell the guys.

20:57.256 --> 20:59.008
Here you go.

21:00.843 --> 21:02.386
Hello, sir.

21:02.470 --> 21:04.388
- Who are you?
- Oh, right.

21:04.472 --> 21:07.600
I sent you a text,
but I didn't get a reply.

21:07.683 --> 21:09.894
So I took the liberty
of coming to see you.

21:11.729 --> 21:12.730
Well…

21:13.397 --> 21:15.941
I'm with Daeheung Citizens FC.

21:16.692 --> 21:19.111
We're the soccer team
based here in Daeheung.

21:20.196 --> 21:21.739
I was wondering

21:21.822 --> 21:24.325
if you'd be inclined
to be our team's main sponsor.

21:24.408 --> 21:26.452
- No, we're good.
- Wait, sir!

21:27.119 --> 21:29.747
Please just take a look
and think about it.

21:30.289 --> 21:34.251
Your company name
would be right here on our uniforms.

21:34.335 --> 21:36.879
It'll really help your company's image
in the local community.

21:36.962 --> 21:39.590
And it'll really boost employee morale--

21:39.673 --> 21:40.966
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

21:41.050 --> 21:42.051
Yes, I'm going.

21:42.134 --> 21:44.845
Sir! I'll text you the details!

21:45.471 --> 21:46.847
What did Coach say?

21:46.931 --> 21:48.015
He said to go home.

21:48.641 --> 21:50.434
- That there's no training today.
- What?

21:50.518 --> 21:52.394
But we have an away game this weekend.

21:53.020 --> 21:55.064
Don't we need to prepare for it at all?

21:55.689 --> 21:58.400
I know. We really should train today.

21:59.819 --> 22:01.487
Do you want me to open it?

22:02.571 --> 22:03.572
Hey.

22:04.073 --> 22:05.783
We saw you at Si-yeol's place yesterday.

22:05.866 --> 22:08.035
- Hello.
- Hello.

22:08.118 --> 22:11.205
What a coincidence. You must live nearby.

22:11.288 --> 22:14.667
We came to train, but the gate's locked.

22:18.379 --> 22:19.380
That scared me.

22:20.005 --> 22:20.881
What the…

22:20.965 --> 22:22.424
This just…

22:23.342 --> 22:24.343
It's open.

22:25.094 --> 22:25.970
What?

22:27.137 --> 22:30.182
Maybe this lock is defective.

22:30.266 --> 22:31.809
It was definitely locked earlier.

22:37.231 --> 22:40.276
Shouldn't we go in
and train by ourselves at least?

22:44.488 --> 22:45.573
Hey.

22:47.992 --> 22:49.159
Lock it again.

22:51.662 --> 22:53.789
Hurry up and lock it!

22:57.418 --> 23:01.046
As you can see, training's off,
so we're heading out to grab a bite.

23:01.130 --> 23:02.423
Have you eaten yet?

23:14.977 --> 23:15.853
Hey, Si-yeol.

23:17.146 --> 23:18.731
Hey…

23:19.732 --> 23:20.941
Are you okay?

23:22.735 --> 23:23.861
Yeah.

23:23.944 --> 23:26.989
I'm fine.
I just need to rest for a few days.

23:29.450 --> 23:30.868
Come on in.

23:30.951 --> 23:32.912
Oh, okay.

23:43.672 --> 23:45.132
You came together?

23:46.800 --> 23:47.843
The thing is--

23:47.927 --> 23:50.471
I know. My memories came back.

23:52.222 --> 23:54.391
I know she's now human,

23:54.475 --> 23:56.977
and that's why you can't switch
your life back.

23:58.228 --> 23:59.229
I remember everything now.

24:00.481 --> 24:01.607
Woo-seok.

24:01.690 --> 24:03.192
This has nothing to do with Si-yeol.

24:04.193 --> 24:06.320
I'm the one who had your memories wiped.

24:06.403 --> 24:07.488
I know that too.

24:07.571 --> 24:09.198
I'm not upset about it.

24:10.115 --> 24:11.909
I don't have the right to be.

24:13.494 --> 24:17.081
It's true that I wanted Si-yeol's life,
even for just a moment.

24:21.293 --> 24:24.213
Si-yeol, I don't know
if you'll believe me,

24:25.089 --> 24:27.216
but I didn't intend for this to happen.

24:27.299 --> 24:30.302
You know I'm not that kind of guy.

24:31.053 --> 24:33.472
I just wanted to live like this
for a few days,

24:33.555 --> 24:35.265
then give it all back to you.

24:36.558 --> 24:38.644
But I couldn't stop thinking
about my dad.

24:39.144 --> 24:41.397
So I just started getting greedier.

24:42.106 --> 24:43.232
Honestly, that's how it felt.

24:44.066 --> 24:45.109
I know, man.

24:45.693 --> 24:49.279
I'd be lying if I said
I wasn't a bit upset with you.

24:49.905 --> 24:53.617
But thanks for being honest with me now.

24:53.701 --> 24:54.910
Let's switch back.

24:56.203 --> 24:58.622
- What?
- Let's switch back now.

24:59.498 --> 25:02.209
Didn't you say you found a way?

25:02.292 --> 25:04.211
Back when you erased my memory.

25:04.294 --> 25:07.881
- It's not possible right now.
- Why?

25:08.507 --> 25:09.758
Why isn't it possible now?

25:11.927 --> 25:12.803
Woo-seok.

25:13.971 --> 25:16.181
No, it's just…

25:17.307 --> 25:19.810
It's because I don't trust myself.

25:19.893 --> 25:22.604
If I spend another day or two like this,

25:22.688 --> 25:25.441
I'll start thinking this is my life
and get even greedier.

25:25.524 --> 25:27.818
That's what'll happen.
Can you take responsibility for that?

25:28.444 --> 25:32.990
If I suddenly end up
back in my life overnight,

25:34.033 --> 25:36.410
how am I supposed to handle that?

25:39.204 --> 25:41.457
This is really quite rude, you know.

25:43.417 --> 25:46.336
We came to visit a patient
completely empty-handed.

25:47.171 --> 25:48.047
What?

25:48.130 --> 25:49.757
Go buy something, Si-yeol.

25:50.257 --> 25:53.010
Do you like fruit?
Go get a fruit basket or something.

25:54.136 --> 25:55.220
- Now?
- Yes.

25:57.556 --> 25:59.641
I hate humans

26:00.476 --> 26:02.352
who are rude.

26:17.743 --> 26:21.038
You know it too, don't you?
That you're going to die soon.

26:23.665 --> 26:26.043
- How did you--
- Keep it a secret from Si-yeol.

26:26.126 --> 26:29.630
He cares about you more than I thought.

26:29.713 --> 26:31.632
It's more than you deserve.

26:32.257 --> 26:35.302
So you better hide
that you have ulterior motives.

26:35.385 --> 26:37.096
Don't let him catch you like I just did.

26:43.393 --> 26:45.562
I still can't believe I'm even doing this,

26:47.272 --> 26:49.149
but I want to protect him.

26:49.900 --> 26:53.112
If he believes in something
as cheesy as friendship,

26:53.195 --> 26:55.405
I want to keep it that way.

26:56.365 --> 26:57.616
Then…

26:59.952 --> 27:01.787
you want me to just die?

27:03.580 --> 27:05.249
Without doing anything?

27:05.916 --> 27:06.959
Instead of Si-yeol?

27:08.085 --> 27:11.547
If you don't want that,
make a deal with me.

27:14.216 --> 27:16.093
- A deal?
- Yes.

27:16.176 --> 27:19.263
I don't have much time either.
Just like you.

27:20.472 --> 27:22.724
So I need you to help me.

27:39.992 --> 27:42.786
By the way,
this isn't a restaurant, is it?

27:45.038 --> 27:48.292
Eating black bean noodles
at a pool hall is the best.

27:48.375 --> 27:49.585
Haven't you tried it?

27:50.210 --> 27:51.295
No.

27:51.378 --> 27:53.672
We made a bet on this two-on-two match.

27:54.256 --> 27:57.718
After I win, I'll treat you to noodles
and sweet and sour pork, the full spread.

27:58.802 --> 27:59.970
Sounds good.

28:00.053 --> 28:01.638
- Your turn.
- Okay!

28:04.016 --> 28:06.351
All right.

28:25.621 --> 28:26.830
Damn.

28:27.372 --> 28:29.541
I guess I picked a shot
that's way too hard.

28:31.210 --> 28:32.544
Or… maybe not?

28:39.259 --> 28:40.302
Si-yeol.

28:40.844 --> 28:42.054
Eun-ho.

28:42.137 --> 28:43.263
Why are you out here?

28:43.347 --> 28:44.640
Let's go.

28:44.723 --> 28:46.600
Wait, what about the fruit basket?

28:47.226 --> 28:49.102
Visiting hours are over. Let's just go.

28:49.186 --> 28:52.564
But I went all the way
to the store to buy this.

28:52.648 --> 28:53.565
We can't just leave.

28:53.649 --> 28:56.193
Why not? Just get a refund.

28:56.276 --> 28:58.487
Why did you even make me
go buy this anyway?

28:58.570 --> 29:02.074
You kept the receipt, right?
I know they'll definitely refund you.

29:03.283 --> 29:04.201
What?

29:10.457 --> 29:13.710
Beom, we're going to lose at this rate.

29:13.794 --> 29:15.796
Oh man, this is bad.

29:15.879 --> 29:17.422
I'm totally broke until next month.

29:18.048 --> 29:20.759
Jeong-bae's going to order
egg-battered fried meatballs.

29:20.842 --> 29:22.511
He's got such expensive taste.

29:22.594 --> 29:24.429
What do we do? I'm broke too.

29:30.227 --> 29:31.311
Excuse me.

29:32.771 --> 29:33.647
Yes?

29:34.273 --> 29:35.816
Can I give it a try?

29:35.899 --> 29:38.735
Have you ever played pool before?

29:39.278 --> 29:41.571
No, never.

29:41.655 --> 29:43.657
But I think I get how it works.

29:47.286 --> 29:49.955
What do we do? We're already losing.

29:51.081 --> 29:52.708
We can't make a comeback anyway.

29:52.791 --> 29:55.043
She came all this way,
so let's just let her play.

29:55.127 --> 29:56.962
Oh man.

30:06.388 --> 30:09.349
You shouldn't hold it like that.

30:09.433 --> 30:13.437
Here, do it like this. Right.

30:14.855 --> 30:15.814
Hold it like this

30:16.898 --> 30:18.525
and bend down a little.

30:18.608 --> 30:20.402
Right, just like that.

30:22.237 --> 30:23.905
- Good.
- Okay.

30:24.740 --> 30:26.033
Can I hit it now?

30:26.116 --> 30:28.702
Yeah, give it a shot.

30:28.785 --> 30:29.703
Here goes.

30:44.009 --> 30:46.011
How is that angle even possible?

30:49.056 --> 30:50.057
I can go again, right?

30:50.682 --> 30:52.476
Sure. Go ahead.

31:16.541 --> 31:17.959
What the…

31:20.379 --> 31:21.505
Is she a pro or something?

31:21.588 --> 31:25.258
No, she said it's her first time playing.

31:26.051 --> 31:27.636
She's so cool.

31:36.937 --> 31:38.980
- We won!
- We did it!

31:44.277 --> 31:45.570
Is it heavy?

31:46.655 --> 31:47.697
A little.

31:47.781 --> 31:49.741
Think of it as a workout.
You like exercising.

31:49.825 --> 31:52.327
You have an answer for everything.

31:52.411 --> 31:54.788
Hey, aren't you going
to team training today?

31:54.871 --> 31:58.500
They called earlier
and said the practice is canceled.

31:58.583 --> 32:00.460
The team's in a bad spot right now.

32:01.253 --> 32:05.006
Coach said he'd find
a new sponsor somehow,

32:05.757 --> 32:07.676
but I don't think it's working out.

32:07.759 --> 32:09.010
Really?

32:10.554 --> 32:11.763
Since we're on the topic,

32:12.973 --> 32:15.392
you know our trip this weekend?

32:15.475 --> 32:17.561
I don't think that's going to happen.

32:17.644 --> 32:19.020
Why not?

32:19.855 --> 32:22.899
Well, usually for away games,
we head there a day early,

32:22.983 --> 32:26.611
stay the night,
play our match, and then come back.

32:26.695 --> 32:29.114
But since the team's broke right now,

32:29.197 --> 32:33.243
we'll have to leave at the crack of dawn
and come straight back after the game.

32:33.869 --> 32:36.246
So if you come, you'll just be exhausted,

32:36.997 --> 32:38.748
and we won't have time to hang out.

32:38.832 --> 32:42.586
So basically, it's a money problem.

32:43.628 --> 32:44.546
Yeah.

32:46.047 --> 32:47.424
We're here.

32:47.507 --> 32:49.259
OH SEASON GROCERY STORE

32:49.342 --> 32:50.218
What the…

32:50.302 --> 32:53.472
Of all places, why did it have to be here?

32:54.097 --> 32:55.140
Do you know this place?

32:55.849 --> 32:57.017
I told you yesterday.

32:57.100 --> 32:59.978
They worked me to the bone all day,
then threw me out and into debt.

33:00.520 --> 33:03.148
This is that shady store.

33:03.773 --> 33:04.900
What?

33:04.983 --> 33:07.694
I couldn't believe it
when you told me yesterday.

33:07.777 --> 33:10.489
Since when do you just let people
walk all over you?

33:10.572 --> 33:12.282
What choice did I have?
They wouldn't pay me.

33:12.365 --> 33:14.159
Eun-ho, don't worry.

33:14.242 --> 33:17.204
I'll make sure you get paid for your work.

33:17.913 --> 33:19.831
- Really?
- Of course.

33:19.915 --> 33:21.124
What kind of people are they?

33:21.208 --> 33:24.044
Scamming you
because you don't know any better.

33:25.504 --> 33:27.255
Just wait right here.

33:32.344 --> 33:34.513
- I'd like to return this.
- Of course, sir.

33:34.596 --> 33:36.306
And I'd like to speak to the manager.

33:37.265 --> 33:38.683
Why do you want to speak to…

33:38.767 --> 33:40.560
Is there a problem, sir?

33:40.644 --> 33:42.521
Well, yesterday…

33:44.523 --> 33:45.732
Wait, Yeon-su?

33:47.442 --> 33:49.528
Do I know you?

33:49.611 --> 33:50.779
Well…

33:54.574 --> 33:57.661
It feels pretty reassuring
to have Si-yeol stepping up.

34:00.664 --> 34:01.748
Si-yeol!

34:02.249 --> 34:03.416
Hey, Eun-ho.

34:05.252 --> 34:06.503
Over there.

34:07.254 --> 34:09.047
What's going on here?

34:11.550 --> 34:14.177
What's going on with you two?
Since when do you two know each other?

34:14.261 --> 34:16.930
Turns out, she's an old friend
from way back.

34:17.556 --> 34:20.308
I never dreamed I'd run into her here.

34:20.934 --> 34:22.852
- An old friend?
- Yeah.

34:23.520 --> 34:26.565
How did you recognize me right away?

34:26.648 --> 34:29.317
It's been nine years.

34:29.901 --> 34:31.570
Of course I did.

34:31.653 --> 34:35.031
You really helped me out back then.

34:36.157 --> 34:38.368
Me? Helping you out?

34:39.786 --> 34:41.037
Si-yeol.

34:43.540 --> 34:46.918
You said you'd fight for me. What is this?

34:47.002 --> 34:49.588
She's the one who ripped me off.

34:49.671 --> 34:51.131
I know that,

34:51.214 --> 34:52.882
but I don't think I can help you.

34:53.925 --> 34:54.968
What?

34:55.051 --> 34:57.429
I told you, I know her well.

34:58.096 --> 34:59.389
Oh, right.

35:00.015 --> 35:01.683
We were just about to go grab lunch.

35:01.766 --> 35:03.226
You're okay with that, right?

35:03.768 --> 35:04.644
"We"?

35:04.728 --> 35:06.438
Yeah, Yeon-su and…

35:07.022 --> 35:08.231
Oh, there she is.

35:09.107 --> 35:10.483
Yeon-su!

35:10.567 --> 35:11.610
Hello.

35:11.693 --> 35:13.445
Yeah, hi.

35:14.654 --> 35:16.948
So, what should we eat?

35:24.456 --> 35:27.000
NOBLE AROM BILLIARDS CLUB

35:41.765 --> 35:43.099
This is so good!

35:47.020 --> 35:48.730
You've got something right there.

35:48.813 --> 35:49.689
Do I?

35:58.114 --> 35:59.074
Hey.

36:00.283 --> 36:03.286
Try the egg-battered fried meatballs too.

36:03.370 --> 36:04.245
Okay.

36:05.538 --> 36:06.748
Thank you.

36:11.670 --> 36:13.338
This is good too.

36:18.009 --> 36:19.469
You should try this too, Beom.

36:20.303 --> 36:22.138
Oh, I have.

36:23.390 --> 36:24.516
Thank you.

36:28.770 --> 36:30.188
What is with this vibe?

36:30.980 --> 36:32.148
It's a total disaster.

36:46.955 --> 36:48.081
Eat up, Yeon-su.

36:48.581 --> 36:50.417
Yes, you too, Si-yeol.

36:53.962 --> 36:55.004
Oh, right.

36:55.547 --> 36:57.882
Don't you prefer wheat rice cakes
over regular ones?

36:58.591 --> 37:02.095
I can't tell if these are wheat rice cakes
or regular ones.

37:03.054 --> 37:05.890
How did you know what I like?

37:07.976 --> 37:09.310
Oh, that.

37:11.062 --> 37:12.814
I just figured you might.

37:14.607 --> 37:16.192
This is definitely wheat.

37:16.818 --> 37:19.154
I prefer rice cakes.

37:19.654 --> 37:20.530
That's odd.

37:21.406 --> 37:22.866
Were we that close?

37:23.950 --> 37:26.244
Even my husband doesn't know
I prefer wheat rice cakes.

37:27.036 --> 37:28.371
You're married?

37:29.122 --> 37:30.457
Of course. I have two kids.

37:31.458 --> 37:34.919
Anyway, Si-yeol,
you're still playing, right?

37:35.545 --> 37:37.213
Is it okay for me to ask you that?

37:37.297 --> 37:38.840
Of course.

37:39.466 --> 37:40.550
I'm just getting by.

37:40.633 --> 37:43.470
Back then, I really thought

37:43.553 --> 37:46.264
you should've made
the youth national team.

37:47.182 --> 37:50.769
I saw so much more potential in you.

37:52.645 --> 37:54.147
Yeah, well.

37:54.230 --> 37:56.524
Things just turned out this way.

37:57.150 --> 37:58.693
But why are you working at that store?

37:58.777 --> 38:00.445
You're so talented.

38:01.279 --> 38:04.282
Talented? I'm just a middle-aged woman.

38:04.365 --> 38:06.993
No way. Yeon-su is super talented.

38:07.076 --> 38:09.329
We get foreign customers at the store,

38:09.412 --> 38:11.372
and she speaks French and German.

38:11.998 --> 38:14.501
She even negotiates all our supply prices.

38:14.584 --> 38:17.086
Sales doubled since she started working.

38:17.170 --> 38:19.839
Hye-rim, please. You're making me blush.

38:21.591 --> 38:26.346
When I was working my old job,
I thought I was the best at it.

38:26.888 --> 38:31.267
But when I got married,
had kids, and quit,

38:31.935 --> 38:36.022
it wasn't easy to go back to work
after raising my kids.

38:36.648 --> 38:38.566
You know, a gap in my resume.

38:42.445 --> 38:43.738
Then, Yeon-su,

38:44.322 --> 38:46.574
could you help our team out?

38:48.034 --> 38:49.202
What?

38:49.285 --> 38:52.664
Our team's in a bit of trouble,
so we need a new sponsor.

38:53.164 --> 38:54.749
Could you help us with that?

38:56.000 --> 38:58.837
It'd be a chance for you
to get back into this industry.

38:58.920 --> 39:00.547
I think it'd be good for you.

39:00.630 --> 39:04.717
You're the best
at scouting and negotiating.

39:06.928 --> 39:08.471
- I am?
- Yes.

39:21.025 --> 39:22.318
Jeez.

39:31.286 --> 39:32.662
Wait here.

39:33.621 --> 39:34.664
Yes, sir.

39:50.179 --> 39:51.222
Man.

39:51.890 --> 39:54.767
Why did you drag me out at this hour?

39:56.644 --> 39:59.480
I wouldn't sell this
for all the gold in the world.

40:00.106 --> 40:02.942
Cut the crap.
A merchant sells for the right price.

40:03.026 --> 40:05.278
I'm saying this
because this thing is cursed.

40:05.361 --> 40:10.533
It bewitches all, even spirits,
but it devours human life.

40:12.785 --> 40:16.789
However, you have no life left to devour.

40:17.415 --> 40:18.541
Fine. Take it.

40:21.127 --> 40:22.962
What? Just hand it over?

40:23.796 --> 40:25.214
Yeah.

40:25.298 --> 40:27.675
You're acting like it's yours.

40:36.184 --> 40:39.395
Two billion won in cash, as agreed.

40:40.897 --> 40:42.440
Count it if you want.

40:43.524 --> 40:44.651
It's fine.

41:03.544 --> 41:06.714
It's cursed, so open it outside.

41:07.382 --> 41:08.925
Don't do it in here.

41:09.634 --> 41:10.718
Sure.

41:22.105 --> 41:24.190
- Thanks for lunch.
- Of course.

41:24.273 --> 41:26.150
I'll treat you next time, Yeon-su.

41:26.234 --> 41:28.319
I'll take you somewhere better.

41:29.112 --> 41:30.780
Sure, let's do that. How much?

41:31.656 --> 41:33.241
There won't be a next time.

41:33.324 --> 41:35.785
I'll pay, so make this
the last time you meet up.

41:36.411 --> 41:37.870
Hey, wait.

41:37.954 --> 41:38.830
You're paying?

41:38.913 --> 41:40.498
With what money?

41:40.581 --> 41:42.500
You gave me all the money
from the AC yesterday.

41:43.126 --> 41:45.044
Did I not tell you?

41:45.128 --> 41:47.088
We don't have to worry
about money anymore.

41:47.171 --> 41:48.339
What?

41:54.637 --> 41:55.513
Hey!

41:56.431 --> 41:57.640
What was that?

41:58.182 --> 41:59.350
Can't you tell?

41:59.434 --> 42:02.103
It's a no-limit credit card. A black card.

42:02.186 --> 42:05.148
I mean, where did you get it?

42:05.231 --> 42:06.899
I took it from Woo-seok.

42:07.525 --> 42:08.901
What?

42:08.985 --> 42:11.279
Excuse me, you left this.

42:11.362 --> 42:12.697
That must be mine.

42:16.367 --> 42:18.578
- Here you go.
- A black card.

42:25.835 --> 42:29.505
Man, why didn't I think of that sooner?

42:33.176 --> 42:35.762
Woo-seok's money is basically my money.

42:36.304 --> 42:40.058
With that card,
I'll never have to worry about money.

42:40.141 --> 42:42.602
You two seemed very friendly.

42:42.685 --> 42:44.062
Real sweet.

42:44.687 --> 42:45.563
What?

42:49.400 --> 42:51.194
"Eun-ho, don't worry."

42:51.277 --> 42:53.780
"I'll make sure
you get paid for your work."

42:54.739 --> 42:56.657
Then what was it you said again?

42:57.283 --> 42:59.702
"Don't you prefer wheat rice cakes
over regular ones?"

42:59.786 --> 43:04.207
"But why are you working at that store?
You're so talented."

43:05.541 --> 43:08.002
Hey, I was working there yesterday too!

43:09.629 --> 43:13.466
Eun-ho, it's not what you think.

43:13.549 --> 43:18.805
She worked me to the bone all day,
stiffed me, and treated me like dirt.

43:19.555 --> 43:21.933
How could you take her side
right in front of me?

43:22.016 --> 43:24.685
What was she again? An old friend?

43:27.105 --> 43:29.899
Are you jealous right now?

43:29.982 --> 43:31.609
Well, I prefer regular rice cakes!

43:31.692 --> 43:34.320
Okay, I'm sorry.

43:34.403 --> 43:36.614
Next time, let's get rice cakes.

43:37.323 --> 43:38.449
Whatever.

43:39.033 --> 43:41.577
How do you make me feel
this petty at my age?

43:41.661 --> 43:43.162
It's pathetic.

43:48.209 --> 43:49.502
I'm sorry.

43:51.295 --> 43:53.381
I made you so upset.

43:55.716 --> 43:59.095
I'm not a child.
Coddling me won't make me feel better.

44:00.638 --> 44:02.598
I really am sorry.

44:03.266 --> 44:04.350
Okay?

44:06.811 --> 44:10.690
I just ran into Yeon-su
when I least expected it,

44:11.357 --> 44:14.569
so I was glad to see her
but also felt bad.

44:14.652 --> 44:15.903
That's why I acted that way.

44:16.696 --> 44:17.780
Okay?

44:19.490 --> 44:22.243
Why did you feel bad?

44:23.828 --> 44:25.121
Well,

44:25.621 --> 44:29.333
before my fate was switched,
Yeon-su was actually my agent.

44:29.417 --> 44:34.589
She was one of Forbes'
30 Most Influential Women.

44:34.672 --> 44:37.466
She was very successful.

44:38.092 --> 44:41.762
But now she's working a temp job
at a local grocery store.

44:43.014 --> 44:44.807
She was an agent?

44:45.766 --> 44:49.312
No wonder nothing I said worked on her.

44:49.896 --> 44:51.439
Exactly.

44:51.522 --> 44:54.275
There's a reason I gave up
on getting that money back.

44:55.151 --> 44:58.154
You just can't win an argument with her.

44:58.237 --> 45:00.948
Even top club chairmen
in the big leagues absolutely shudder

45:01.032 --> 45:04.952
when they sit down
at the negotiating table with her.

45:06.871 --> 45:12.168
So a woman that successful
had her career cut short

45:13.169 --> 45:15.713
because I switched your fate?

45:18.674 --> 45:21.219
I suppose so.

45:23.262 --> 45:26.599
She started out
as a football association employee,

45:26.682 --> 45:29.393
then met me and became an agent.

45:30.436 --> 45:32.438
Anyway, it's kind of surprising.

45:33.231 --> 45:36.525
She used to be too busy
to even meet anyone,

45:36.609 --> 45:38.653
so she never got married.

45:39.195 --> 45:42.281
But now she suddenly has two kids.

45:44.825 --> 45:48.871
Relationships often change
a person's fate.

45:49.622 --> 45:52.333
Meeting the right person
at the right time.

45:53.584 --> 45:55.753
Nothing in life is
more important than that.

45:59.048 --> 46:00.007
What?

46:03.052 --> 46:05.721
You're the only one who would call me.

46:14.480 --> 46:15.940
That's my number.

46:16.023 --> 46:18.859
Right, your phones
must've gotten mixed up.

46:22.238 --> 46:23.864
- Hello?
- Ok-sun?

46:24.573 --> 46:25.783
Where are you right now?

46:25.866 --> 46:27.660
I'll come get the phone right away.

46:28.411 --> 46:31.122
Oh, it's you, Hye-rim.

46:33.708 --> 46:36.043
What's taking her so long?

46:38.963 --> 46:40.631
Wait a second.

46:40.715 --> 46:43.175
I feel like I've seen this guy somewhere.

46:43.259 --> 46:44.302
What?

46:45.344 --> 46:46.762
Oh yeah.

46:47.388 --> 46:49.598
This guy looks kind of familiar.

46:51.934 --> 46:52.893
You too?

46:55.813 --> 46:56.897
Ok-sun!

47:07.658 --> 47:09.285
Damn, what do I do?

47:09.368 --> 47:10.995
There's no one around, right?

47:11.078 --> 47:13.914
Yes. I secretly took a company car out,

47:14.540 --> 47:16.917
- and made a mistake--
- You're lying.

47:20.671 --> 47:21.964
That man.

47:23.424 --> 47:25.593
The driver from Geumsu Group.

47:27.636 --> 47:28.888
What?

47:35.478 --> 47:37.271
A human has died.

47:37.813 --> 47:39.190
Because of you.

47:39.732 --> 47:43.110
Because you twisted human fate recklessly,

47:43.194 --> 47:47.323
someone who wasn't
supposed to die has died.

47:49.909 --> 47:51.077
Ok-sun!

47:53.329 --> 47:55.414
Who is this guy?

47:55.498 --> 47:56.999
That's my family photo.

47:57.083 --> 47:59.627
We took it a long time ago,
when Dad was still alive.

48:26.987 --> 48:29.031
I asked around,

48:29.115 --> 48:31.784
and they say
Hye-rim's nickname is Hermione.

48:31.867 --> 48:33.119
Hermione?

48:34.328 --> 48:36.914
I don't know what that means.

48:36.997 --> 48:39.333
But apparently, she works
every part-time job around here,

48:39.959 --> 48:42.211
so all the shop owners call her that.

48:42.294 --> 48:45.381
They said it's like
she has 48 hours in a day.

48:47.842 --> 48:50.553
Just working at the grocery store
was exhausting enough.

48:50.636 --> 48:53.180
But she delivers milk in the morning,
works at a cafe before noon,

48:53.264 --> 48:55.182
and then at the grocery store
in the afternoon?

48:56.142 --> 48:57.435
That's not all.

48:57.935 --> 49:00.062
Hey, not there! Come up!

49:00.146 --> 49:01.105
Damn.

49:01.981 --> 49:04.150
I can't see!

49:04.233 --> 49:06.861
- You died because you were there.
- Oh man.

49:09.989 --> 49:12.575
She also works
at a nearby internet cafe on weekends.

49:16.245 --> 49:19.165
If you work yourself to the bone now,
you'll pay for it later.

49:19.707 --> 49:22.835
Why is she working herself to death?

49:22.918 --> 49:25.546
I actually asked her about that.

49:33.679 --> 49:35.598
My dad didn't deserve to die that way,

49:35.681 --> 49:37.516
and my mom suffered
a breakdown from the shock.

49:37.600 --> 49:39.059
So I'm the breadwinner of our family.

49:39.685 --> 49:43.022
Medical bills keep piling up,
and I want to finish college.

49:43.689 --> 49:46.150
So I need to save up money fast.

49:48.861 --> 49:50.696
So, what are you going to do?

49:51.405 --> 49:53.032
What do you think?

49:53.115 --> 49:55.743
You said her life
got screwed up because of me.

49:56.243 --> 49:57.453
Then I should make it right.

50:04.043 --> 50:05.461
A scholarship?

50:05.544 --> 50:07.922
But do students on leave
even get scholarships?

50:08.422 --> 50:10.508
Technically, no.

50:10.591 --> 50:15.221
But through the newly established
Eunho Scholarship Foundation,

50:15.304 --> 50:18.390
you were selected as the first recipient.

50:20.100 --> 50:23.479
I never applied for that. So how am I…

50:23.562 --> 50:27.775
You were chosen based on strict criteria,
so you don't need to worry about that.

50:28.275 --> 50:30.194
You'll receive
full tuition until you graduate,

50:30.277 --> 50:32.071
a monthly stipend of five million won,

50:32.154 --> 50:34.323
plus an allowance
to study a language during break,

50:34.406 --> 50:37.952
and full funding
to study abroad after graduation.

50:39.411 --> 50:40.371
Why?

50:40.454 --> 50:42.122
Because you were selected.

50:42.206 --> 50:43.958
SAEGANG UNIVERSITY

50:46.043 --> 50:48.254
Thank you so much.

50:49.171 --> 50:50.381
Thank you.

50:50.464 --> 50:53.259
You think she's doing a good job
with the scholarship thing?

50:53.342 --> 50:55.386
Of course. It's not like it's hard.

50:55.469 --> 50:58.013
Fixing everything at once
would be too overwhelming,

50:58.097 --> 50:59.890
so we'll just do this much for now.

51:00.432 --> 51:03.477
Next month, we'll fix up her house
and pay her mom's hospital bills.

51:04.520 --> 51:05.771
I think we should.

51:05.854 --> 51:06.855
Yeah.

51:06.939 --> 51:11.068
If he were alive, I'm sure
he'd want to do that for his daughter.

51:12.903 --> 51:15.990
By the way,
my grandma was so happy yesterday.

51:17.533 --> 51:18.993
Oh, that.

51:20.452 --> 51:22.329
We've got money now,
so I figured I'd spend some.

51:22.413 --> 51:24.164
We always went empty-handed before.

51:24.248 --> 51:27.334
Everyone at the nursing home thinks
I married into a billionaire family.

51:28.043 --> 51:30.045
You gave gifts to everyone
at the nursing home

51:30.129 --> 51:32.548
and prepared all kinds of food.

51:32.631 --> 51:34.633
My grandma became a celebrity there.

51:35.759 --> 51:38.262
Generosity comes from a full stomach.

51:38.345 --> 51:40.723
You've got to grease the wheels a bit,

51:40.806 --> 51:42.349
so even if she loses at cards,

51:42.433 --> 51:44.977
she'll still get some money back.

51:46.687 --> 51:48.981
This is just one of those life lessons.

51:50.524 --> 51:51.859
Thank you.

51:51.942 --> 51:54.153
I hadn't even thought about that.

51:56.322 --> 51:58.198
Technically, it's all your money anyway.

52:00.492 --> 52:03.203
If she was that happy,
we can go again tomorrow.

52:04.872 --> 52:06.498
I can't tomorrow.

52:07.333 --> 52:08.417
I have an away game.

52:09.585 --> 52:10.794
Right.

52:10.878 --> 52:13.797
I'll be back really quick,
so just wait a bit.

52:16.300 --> 52:18.552
What do you mean? We're going together.

52:18.636 --> 52:20.346
We agreed to travel after the game.

52:21.263 --> 52:23.015
What? That was--

52:23.098 --> 52:26.018
Wasn't it because the team was broke
that you were going early in the morning

52:26.101 --> 52:27.936
and coming back straight after the game?

52:28.562 --> 52:30.105
But we have plenty of money now.

52:31.065 --> 52:32.399
Let's go on a trip.

52:32.483 --> 52:33.484
We got a black card.

52:48.248 --> 52:49.249
What is this?

52:50.376 --> 52:52.836
It's a bus. I chartered it.

52:54.672 --> 52:56.340
Coach, she's from overseas.

52:56.423 --> 52:57.841
She forgets to use honorifics.

52:59.468 --> 53:01.512
Anyway, since the away game is tomorrow,

53:01.595 --> 53:04.306
wouldn't it be better
if we all head down there now?

53:07.518 --> 53:10.020
I guess that's true,

53:10.104 --> 53:14.233
but we don't have a place
for all of us to sleep.

53:14.316 --> 53:16.985
I took care of that too, so don't worry.

53:18.696 --> 53:21.365
Oh, and this.

53:22.408 --> 53:23.409
What's this?

53:24.118 --> 53:25.536
We owe you from last time.

53:25.619 --> 53:27.413
Reimbursement for the towing fee.

53:32.209 --> 53:34.795
But why are you giving me so much?

53:34.878 --> 53:36.547
I added some generous interest.

53:37.172 --> 53:39.550
Anyway, why are you all
just standing there?

53:40.175 --> 53:41.552
Aren't we going?

53:44.555 --> 53:46.640
I'm not sure what to do.

54:00.070 --> 54:01.113
Yes?

54:03.699 --> 54:05.242
What did you say?

54:08.036 --> 54:09.663
Yes, okay!

54:09.747 --> 54:12.750
Sir, can you please… pull over?

54:13.375 --> 54:14.293
Hurry!

54:26.805 --> 54:29.224
Hey, Coach!

54:30.058 --> 54:32.102
Where are you going?

54:32.186 --> 54:33.604
Right, Si-yeol.

54:33.687 --> 54:35.939
Something urgent came up.

54:36.023 --> 54:39.151
I have to go somewhere,
so you guys head down first.

54:39.234 --> 54:41.069
Then what about tomorrow's game?

54:41.737 --> 54:43.614
Well, the game…

54:43.697 --> 54:46.742
I'll handle my business
and head there at dawn or something.

54:46.825 --> 54:48.327
- Just go.
- But…

54:48.410 --> 54:50.788
Hey, taxi! Taxi!

54:51.413 --> 54:52.331
But…

54:55.751 --> 54:57.961
Take charge, all right?

55:00.589 --> 55:01.632
Wait.

55:03.634 --> 55:05.093
What the heck?

55:23.362 --> 55:27.366
I called the coach, and he's on his way.

55:27.449 --> 55:29.493
Really? That's good.

55:38.502 --> 55:41.964
If you don't mind,
can I ask you something?

55:42.589 --> 55:44.800
Sure, go ahead.

55:44.883 --> 55:48.554
I admit we were looking
everywhere for sponsors,

55:49.263 --> 55:52.766
but I never expected a huge company
like yours to step up.

55:52.850 --> 55:54.893
Why would a huge conglomerate
like Geumsu Group

55:55.519 --> 55:59.106
suddenly decide to sponsor
a fourth-division soccer team?

55:59.731 --> 56:02.818
Well…

56:03.485 --> 56:06.697
Because it interests me.
In more ways than one.

56:16.373 --> 56:18.375
Looks like no one's here today.

56:25.215 --> 56:27.175
It seems like
they're traveling pretty far.

56:27.801 --> 56:30.512
I'll stop by home, then go follow them.

56:45.527 --> 56:47.446
Excuse me, who are you?

56:48.864 --> 56:50.449
I didn't expect to find

56:52.200 --> 56:56.038
another one hiding in a place like this.

57:09.176 --> 57:10.886
What is that?

57:10.969 --> 57:12.930
This is called a vajra bell.

57:14.681 --> 57:18.810
It channels divine energy,
so it's not meant to be used by humans.

57:21.647 --> 57:25.400
But as you see, I've devoured
countless minor spirits and deities.

57:26.526 --> 57:28.320
So, I thought

57:29.446 --> 57:31.406
I might try bewitching you with this.

58:08.235 --> 58:10.570
So I'm not making that damn choice.

58:10.654 --> 58:13.782
I'll just stay by his side
and protect him forever.

58:16.493 --> 58:19.705
If the fate of a single human
is but a passing breeze,

58:19.788 --> 58:23.291
then a human life is like a raging storm.

58:24.167 --> 58:27.421
Even if you twist a single strand of fate,

58:27.504 --> 58:31.717
once the storm rises,
everyone gets swept away.

58:32.342 --> 58:36.304
Events you can neither predict nor stop
will come crashing down.

58:36.847 --> 58:41.143
Can you truly handle that for a lifetime?

59:01.872 --> 59:04.041
So this is how it ends.

59:13.425 --> 59:14.509
Eun-ho.

59:18.221 --> 59:19.598
Are you okay?

01:00:02.599 --> 01:00:04.518
SPECIAL APPEARANCE BY HONG SU-HYEON

01:00:29.000 --> 01:00:31.920
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:00:32.003 --> 01:00:35.382
Should we just stay like this
and not go back?

01:00:35.465 --> 01:00:38.718
If you try your best
to change things back and still can't,

01:00:38.802 --> 01:00:40.053
I'll just accept it.

01:00:40.137 --> 01:00:42.973
I bewitched the Seoraksan Mountain fox,
just as planned.

01:00:43.056 --> 01:00:45.851
I heard you're just an ordinary human now.

01:00:45.934 --> 01:00:48.270
I'm going to start by targeting
the people around you.

01:00:48.895 --> 01:00:50.647
- Eun-ho!
- Geum-ho?

01:00:50.730 --> 01:00:53.191
You know the thing I left with you?
My fox bead.

01:00:53.984 --> 01:00:55.277
Where is it?

01:00:58.574 --> 01:01:00.574
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
